# Every text file is LF in the index and LF in the working tree on every
# platform, so a Windows checkout does not hand `R CMD check` CRLF files.
#
# The previous `* text=lf` was silently a no-op: git only accepts `text`,
# `text=auto`, `text=input` or `-text`, and ignores any other value. Nothing
# was normalised, so on Windows (where Git for Windows defaults to
# core.autocrlf=true) `configure.ac` was checked out with CRLF and R-hub's
# windows job failed `checking line endings in shell scripts`.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary payloads must never be line-ending converted. The bundled SUNDIALS
# source tarball is the one that matters - it is what the whole build unpacks,
# and normalising it would corrupt the archive. `text=auto` already detects
# binary content, but the build depends on this, so it is stated explicitly.
*.tar.gz binary
*.gz     binary
*.a      binary
*.o      binary
*.so     binary
*.dll    binary
*.rds    binary
*.RData  binary
*.pdf    binary
*.png    binary
*.jpg    binary
*.ico    binary
